    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Grimes are delighted to bring No. 16 Hillside Close to the market, a stunning three-bedroom home which has been stylishly extended, upgraded and modernised throughout and is presented in immaculate condition.\n\nOccupying an elevated position within this highly sought-after development, the property built c. 1967 enjoys lovely views over Skerries and out towards the sea. The current owners have transformed the property into a beautiful home, with a clever downstairs extension creating an impressive open-plan kitchen, dining and family room. This bright and versatile space is perfect for modern family living and entertaining.\n\nThe ground floor also benefits from a large utility room with direct access to the easterly facing rear garden, adding excellent practicality to the home. Upstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom. The property also benefits from a B-rated BER, off-street parking and an easterly facing rear garden. A cleverly designed lean-to to the side of the property provides excellent additional storage for bins, bikes and other outdoor essentials.\n\nThe location is another major selling point. Skerries train station is less than a 10-minute walk away, making the property particularly convenient for commuters. Holmpatrick shopping facilities are just down the road, with a supermarket, pharmacy and coffee shop providing all the everyday essentials. Skerries town centre is also within easy reach, offering an excellent selection of cafs, restaurants, boutiques, schools, sporting facilities and amenities, together with the beautiful beaches and coastline for which Skerries is renowned.\n\nNo. 16 Hillside Close is a stunning, turnkey family home that has been thoughtfully extended, upgraded and modernised throughout. Combined with its elevated position, beautiful views over Skerries and towards the sea, and excellent location, this is a home that is sure to impress.\n\nFoyer 1.96 m x 0.47 m\nStunning bright entrance hallway with beautiful tiled flooring and new front door\n\nLiving Room 3.86 m x 4.12 m\nPositioned to the front of the property with extra large window overlooking front garden. This spacious room is stylishly finished with feature fireplace and beautiful wooden flooring.\n\nGuest WC 0.75 m x 1.58 m\nUnder stair guest WC with hand basin, tiled flooring and window for light.\n\nKitchen 2.84 m x 3.62 m\nBright kitchen with ample storage units, tiled flooring and access to utility room and dining area.\n\nUtility Room 1.62 m x 2.44 m\nLocated to the rear of the kitchen, plumbed for washing machine. Fitted with ample storage presses. Access to rear garden.\n\nDining Area 3.08 m x 3.69 m\nBeautiful open plan living dining area positioned just off the kitchen with wooden flooring\n\nFamily Room 4.19 m x 4.81 m\nStunning extended family room with high ceilings, and double door access to rear garden.\n\nLanding 1.95 m x 3.21 m\nBright and spacious landing area with access to the three bedrooms, hotpress and attic storage. Finished with carpet flooring.\n\nPrimary Bedroom 3.86 m x 4.48 m\nPositioned to the front of the property, this beautiful bedroom is finished with herringbone flooring and fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 3.86 m x 3.36 m\nPositioned to the rear of the property with herringbone flooring and fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 2.50 m x 2.90 m\nPositioned to front of property with herringbone flooring\n\nFamily Bathroom 1.95 m x 1.63 m\nLovely bright family bathroom with bath, shower, WC, wash hand basin. Fully tiled floor to ceiling with window providing light and ventilation.\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
